.\n- `adversary.rs:109-113` still reads exactly once.\n- The postgres lane of `evidence/eventlog-tls-gate.sh` runs green 5 of 5 under a concurrent full\n  gate on the same machine, or the run count and the load are recorded with the result.\n","owner":"eventlog","status":"draft","summary":"atomic_group.rs:598 red 3/3 at base under load; e603605 drains 2 sites; 10 candidates, 1 non-member, :551 zero-branch hazard open","title":"Postgres tests that read the feed once fail under a held commit watermark"},"lifecycle_state":"draft"}}},"definition":{"create":{"emit":null},"entity":"aep.entity","invariants":[],"lifecycle":{"initial":"recorded","states":["recorded"]},"operations":{"replace":{"arguments":{"additional_fields":false,"fields":{"document":{"acyclic":null,"additional_properties":false,"entity":null,"inverse":null,"items":null,"max":null,"max_length":null,"min":null,"min_length":null,"properties":{},"required":true,"type":"json","values":[]}}},"emits":[],"preconditions":[],"set":{"document":"$args.document"},"transitions":[{"from":"recorded","to":"recorded"}]}},"projections":{},"schema":{"additional_fields":false,"fields":{"document":{"acyclic":null,"additional_properties":false,"entity":null,"inverse":null,"items":null,"max":null,"max_length":null,"min":null,"min_length":null,"properties":{},"required":true,"type":"json","values":[]}}},"version":1},"entity":"aep.entity","events":[],"from_state":null,"id":"01MEM0000000000000002","result":{"entity":"aep.entity","fields":{"document":{"events":[{"args":{"command":"create-entity","data":{"body":"## Outcome\n\nEvery postgres test that asserts on the result of a single `read_feed` either drains with a bounded\nretry (`eventlog_conformance::drain_at_least` or the `feed_at_least` helper) or is shown to be\nimmune to a withheld feed. The case at `crates/eventlog-postgres/src/atomic_group.rs:551` proves\nthat the crash point committed nothing with a positive check, not with a zero-length feed read.\n\n## Why\n\n2026-09-22, 