the first read; the retry returns at once. For those six the assertion\n  is the un-drained single read the patch replaced. The hazard is stated nowhere in the source.\n- `atomic_group.rs:491`: `feed_at_least` returns on `>=`, which turns the exact-count assertion at\n  `:576` into a lower bound. It cannot mask a loss; it can admit a partially visible duplicate.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Each candidate line above is either converted to a bounded drain or annotated in this story's\n  body with the reason it cannot see a withheld feed.\n- `atomic_group.rs:551` asserts the zero-event branch with a positive check that the crash point\n  committed nothing, for all seven crash points.\n- The assertion at `atomic_group.rs:576` is exact again, or the reason a lower bound is correct is\n  written in the test.\n- `adversary.rs:109-113` still reads exactly once.\n- The postgres lane of `evidence/eventlog-tls-gate.sh` runs green 5 of 5 under a concurrent full\n  gate on the same machine, or the run count and the load are recorded with the result.\n","owner":"eventlog","status":"draft","summary":"atomic_group.rs:598 red 3/3 at base under load; e603605 drains 2 sites; 10 candidates, 1 non-member, :551 zero-branch hazard open","title":"Postgres tests that read the feed once fail under a held commit watermark"},"entity":"aep.entity","from_state":null,"id":"01MEM0000000000000002","payload":{"actor":"human:timo","at":1790199548869,"causation":"cmd-child-648c834e6f5b4937add0ef5c0947b0459a099b2aeda7c6bfdfe1a70feca4115b","correlation":"protocol-artifact-new","event_id":"aep.entity:01MEM0000000000000002@1#0~73c9db81e22b2def","executor":null,"recorded_at":"2026-09-23T21:39:08Z"},"revision":1,"to_state":"draft","type":"aep.entity.create/v1","version":1}],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":1790199548869,"id":"01MEM0000000000000002","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/postgres-feed-reads-drain-under-a-held-watermark","provenance":{"created_by":"human:timo","updated_by":